    <paragraph>For the following exercises, find an equation of the tangent line $$y = 3x^{2} + 4x + 1$$ to the graph of the given function at the indicated point. Use a graphing calculator to graph the function and the tangent line.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="118" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>[T] $$\left( {0,1} \right)$$ at $$y = \frac{2}{x^{2}} + 1$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="119" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>[T] $$\left( {1,3} \right)$$ at $$y = \frac{2x}{x - 1}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$T(x)=-4x+7T(x)=-4x+7$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="120" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>[T] $$\left( {-1,1} \right)$$ at $$y = \frac{2}{x} - \frac{3}{x^{2}}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="121" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>[T] $$\left( {1,-1} \right)$$ at $$f(x)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$T(x)=4x-5T(x)=4x-5$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, assume that $$g(x)$$ and $$x.$$ are both differentiable functions for all $$h(x).$$ Find the derivative of each of the functions $$h(x) = 4f(x) + \frac{g(x)}{7}$$</paragraph>
    <exercise number="122" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$h(x) = x^{3}f(x)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="123" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$h(x) = \frac{f(x)g(x)}{2}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$h ′ ( x ) = 3 x 2 f ( x ) + x 3 f ′ ( x ) h ′ ( x ) = 3 x 2 f ( x ) + x 3 f ′ ( x )$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="124" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$h(x) = \frac{3f(x)}{g(x) + 2}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="125" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$h ′ ( x ) = 3 f ′ ( x ) ( g ( x ) + 2 ) - 3 f ( x ) g ′ ( x ) ( g ( x ) + 2 ) 2 h ′ ( x ) = 3 f ′ ( x ) ( g ( x ) + 2 ) - 3 f ( x ) g ′ ( x ) ( g ( x ) + 2 ) 2$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, assume that $$g(x)$$ and $$x$$ are both differentiable functions with values as given in the following table. Use the following table to calculate the following derivatives.</paragraph>
    <table>
      <tbody>
        <row>
          <cell>$$1$$</cell>
          <cell>$$2$$</cell>
          <cell>$$3$$</cell>
          <cell>$$4$$</cell>
          <cell>$$f(x)$$</cell>
        </row>
        <row>
          <cell>$$3$$</cell>
          <cell>$$5$$</cell>
          <cell>$$-2$$</cell>
          <cell>$$0$$</cell>
          <cell>$$g(x)$$</cell>
        </row>
        <row>
          <cell>$$2$$</cell>
          <cell>$$3$$</cell>
          <cell>$$-4$$</cell>
          <cell>$$6$$</cell>
          <cell>$$f^{\prime}(x)$$</cell>
        </row>
        <row>
          <cell>$$-1$$</cell>
          <cell>$$7$$</cell>
          <cell>$$8$$</cell>
          <cell>$$-3$$</cell>
          <cell>$$g^{\prime}(x)$$</cell>
        </row>
        <row>
          <cell>$$4$$</cell>
          <cell>$$1$$</cell>
          <cell>$$2$$</cell>
          <cell>$$9$$</cell>
          <cell>$$h^{\prime}(1)$$</cell>
        </row>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <exercise number="126" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Find $$h(x) = xf(x) + 4g(x).$$ if $$h^{\prime}(2)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="127" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Find $$h(x) = \frac{f(x)}{g(x)}.$$ if $$h^{\prime}(3)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$16 9 16 9$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="128" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Find $$h(x) = 2x + f(x)g(x).$$ if $$h^{\prime}(4)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="129" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Find $$h(x) = \frac{1}{x} + \frac{g(x)}{f(x)}.$$ if $$h(x) = f(x) + g(x).$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>Undefined</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, use the following figure to find the indicated derivatives, if they exist.</paragraph>
