    <exercise number="144" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>A car driving along a freeway with traffic has traveled $$t$$ meters in $$s(t) = \frac{t^{2}}{t^{2} + 2}$$ seconds.</paragraph>
        <list type="ordered">
          <item>Determine the time in seconds when the velocity of the car is 0.</item>
          <item>Determine the acceleration of the car when the velocity is 0.</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="145" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>[T] A herring swimming along a straight line has traveled $$t$$ feet in $$P(t) = \frac{8t + 3}{0.2t^{2} + 1},$$ seconds.</paragraph>
        <paragraph>Determine the velocity of the herring when it has traveled 3 seconds.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$1212112121$$ or 0.0992 ft/s</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="146" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>The population in millions of arctic flounder in the Atlantic Ocean is modeled by the function $$t$$ where $$P^{\prime}(10)$$ is measured in years.</paragraph>
        <list type="ordered">
          <item>Determine the initial flounder population.</item>
          <item>Determine $$t$$ and briefly interpret the result.</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="147" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>[T] The concentration of antibiotic in the bloodstream $$C(t) = \frac{2t^{2} + t}{t^{3} + 50},$$ hours after being injected is given by the function $$C$$ where $$C(t).$$ is measured in milligrams per liter of blood.</paragraph>
        <list type="ordered">
          <item>Find the rate of change of $$t = 8,12,24,$$</item>
          <item>Determine the rate of change for $$36.$$ and $$C(x) = \frac{x^{3} + 2x + 3}{x^{2}},$$</item>
          <item>Briefly describe what seems to be occurring as the number of hours increases.</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>a. $$-2t4-2t3+200t+50(t3+50)2-2t4-2t3+200t+50(t3+50)2$$ b. $$-0.02395-0.02395$$ mg/L-hr, −0.01344 mg/L-hr, −0.003566 mg/L-hr, −0.001579 mg/L-hr c. The rate at which the concentration of drug in the bloodstream decreases is slowing to 0 as time increases.</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="148" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>A book publisher has a cost function given by $$C^{\prime}(2)$$ where x is the number of copies of a book in thousands and C is the cost, per book, measured in dollars. Evaluate $$F$$ and explain its meaning.</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="149" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>[T] According to Newton’s law of universal gravitation, the force $$m_{1}$$ between two bodies of constant mass $$m_{2}$$ and $$F = \frac{Gm_{1}m_{2}}{d^{2}},$$ is given by the formula $$G$$ where $$d$$ is the gravitational constant and $$G,m_{1}, \text{and} m_{2}$$ is the distance between the bodies.</paragraph>
        <list type="ordered">
          <item>Suppose that $$F$$ are constants. Find the rate of change of force $$d.$$ with respect to distance $$F$$</item>
          <item>Find the rate of change of force $$G = 6.67 \times 10^{-11}$$ with gravitational constant $$\text{Nm} ^{2}/ \text{kg} ^{2},$$ $$Nm2/kg2,Nm2/kg2,$$ on two bodies 10 meters apart, each with a mass of 1000 kilograms.</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>a. $$F′(d)=-2Gm1m2d3F′(d)=-2Gm1m2d3$$ b. $$-1.33\times 10-7-1.33\times 10-7$$ N/m</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
